:"GEMIN8","gene_id":"ENSG00000046647","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.413956,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0625632,"nucleus_score":-1.12139,"pct_ad":0.162243,"pct_control":0.169856,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":-0.092415,"donor_lfcse":0.096868,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-1.03276e-05},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"GEMIN8","gene_symbol_current":"GEMIN8","gene_id":"ENSG00000046647","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.000280262,"nucleus_log2fc":0.123664,"nucleus_score":3.7805,"pct_ad":0.185303,"pct_control":0.175228,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.927821,"donor_log2fc":0.0726492,"donor_lfcse":0.126178,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.004789}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000046647","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0566489,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.796936,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000046647","entrez_id":["54960"],"uniprot":["Q9NWZ8"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is part of the SMN complex, which is necessary for spliceosomal snRNP assembly in the cytoplasm and pre-mRNA splicing in the nucleus. The encoded protein binds to both SMN1 and the GEMIN6/GEMIN7 heterodimer, mediating their interaction. This protein is found in nuclear Gemini of Cajal bodies (gems) and in the cytoplasm. Three transcript variants encoding the same protein have been found for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, May 2010].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9NWZ8","text":"The SMN complex catalyzes the assembly of small nuclear ribonucleoproteins (snRNPs), the building blocks of the spliceosome, and thereby plays an important role in the splicing of cellular pre-mRNAs. Most spliceosomal snRNPs contain a common set of Sm proteins SNRPB, SNRPD1, SNRPD2, SNRPD3, SNRPE, SNRPF and SNRPG that assemble in a heptameric protein ring on the Sm site of the small nuclear RNA to form the core snRNP (Sm core). In the cytosol, the Sm proteins SNRPD1, SNRPD2, SNRPE, SNRPF and SNRPG are trapped in an inactive 6S pICln-Sm complex by the chaperone CLNS1A that controls the assembly of the core snRNP. To assemble core snRNPs, the SMN complex accepts the trapped 5Sm proteins from CLNS1A forming an intermediate. Binding of snRNA inside 5Sm triggers eviction of the SMN complex, thereby allowing binding of SNRPD3 and SNRPB to complete assembly of the core snRNP."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}